{"key":"enterprise/T1134.004","id":"T1134.004","name":"Parent PID Spoofing","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1134","tactics":["privilege-escalation","stealth"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may spoof the parent process identifier (PPID) of a new process to evade process-monitoring defenses or to elevate privileges. New processes are typically spawned directly from their parent, or calling, process unless explicitly specified. One way of explicitly assigning the PPID of a new process is via the CreateProcess API call, which supports a parameter that defines the PPID to use. This functionality is used by Windows features…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1134/004","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--93591901-3172-4e94-abf8-6034ab26f44a","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.706Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0021","name":"OS API Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0021","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9bde2f9d-a695-4344-bfac-f2dce13d121e","page":"telemetry/DC0021/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0034","name":"Process Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0034","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--ee575f4a-2d4f-48f6-b18b-89067760adc1","page":"telemetry/DC0034/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0489","name":"Behavior-chain detection for T1134.004 Access Token Manipulation: Parent PID Spoofing (Windows)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0489","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--eb751740-80cd-4ec1-a989-8691bf7f2039","relationship_id":"relationship--b950ec4c-7d64-4184-9161-bcc199117ed2"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1351","name":"Analytic 1351","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0489#AN1351","guidance":"A process explicitly forges its parent using EXTENDED_STARTUPINFO + PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_PARENT_PROCESS (UpdateProcThreadAttribute → CreateProcess[A/W]/CreateProcessAsUserW) or other Native API paths, resulting in **mismatched/implausible lineage** across ETW EventHeader ProcessId, Security 4688 Creator Process ID/Name, and sysmon ParentProcessGuid. Often paired with privilege escalation when the chosen parent runs as SYSTEM.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0489"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4688","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1351","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0489#AN1351","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0021","component":"OS API Execution","name":"etw:Microsoft-Windows-Kernel-Process","channel":"api_call: UpdateProcThreadAttribute (PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_PARENT_PROCESS) and CreateProcess* with EXTENDED_STARTUPINFO_PRESENT / StartupInfoEx","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1351","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0489#AN1351","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0021/"},{"component_id":"DC0034","component":"Process Metadata","name":"etw:Microsoft-Windows-Kernel-Process","channel":"process_start: EventHeader.ProcessId true parent vs reported PPID mismatch","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1351","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0489#AN1351","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0034/"}],"unresolved_references":[],"basis":"ATT&CK detects relationship → detection strategy → analytic → log-source component reference","planning_inputs":[],"visibility":"source_mapped","pla